Make the timed-message preference examples deterministic by using a ttl
comfortably larger than the assertions (a 1s ttl is exceeded by the
setup on a loaded builder). Give the persistent-server retry examples
more time to accept connections, and accept the maintenance
set-client-service echo and its "ok" response in any order.

Independent member connections have no defined completion order. Assert
both.

